# C29 remediation after attempt-01 (7/5/9/6/6, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 verification composed in the presentation; a stored key became Pass; Gateway never read | Verification is a core intent (`verifyTenantSetup{context}`) over a core-owned draft: the core admits the reads it needs through the management pipeline (verify; Gateway workspaces inventory; Red Team; model/skill) and settles each line from the result; lines stream through `ShellSnapshot.setup.verify`. The scan key line is `stored`, an explicit non-result, never `pass`; products without a management client are warnings, never results. Tests: `ui_v2_onboarding` (stored-not-pass, warnings per product), host IPC test, native N03 | `crates/desktop-core/src/authority/setup_domain.rs`, `management_domain.rs` (settle hook), `features.rs` (`VerifyStep`/`VerifyView`), P26 |
| R2 tenant created and selected before completion; Cancel kept it | The wizard works on a draft (`beginTenantSetup`) with its own context; credentials attach to the draft; nothing is listed as a tenant and the active tenant is untouched until `completeTenantSetup` commits it in one step and switches once; `discardTenantSetup` drops the draft and queues its Keychain records for cleanup; a relaunch mid-setup does the same. Tests: core (add mode keeps the shell untouched; discard cleans up; relaunch drops the draft), host, native N05 | `setup_domain.rs`, `authority.rs` (`check_context`, `tenant()`, persisted draft), `store.rs` (`tenant_draft`), P27 |
| R3 Fix and verify again could not repair the profile or a saved client | The profile form stays editable on the draft (`updateTenantSetup`; a new destination or TSG retires the credentials bound to it); saved credentials offer Replace and Remove. Tests: core (`update_setup` retires), boards (R2On04c lands on the editable tenant), native N03 | `wizard.tsx`, `setup_domain.rs` |
| R4 no validation signature or downstream invalidation | The core keeps a signature of the draft's inputs (profile, products, credential records); `setup.verify.stale` and `setup.completable` gate Continue, the rail (steps after Verify) and `completeTenantSetup` itself (refused when stale, unfinished or failed). Tests: core (stale after products/profile change; completion refused), boards R2On04d, native N03 stale path | `setup_domain.rs`, `wizard.tsx` |
| R5 first-run v1 import unreachable | During first run `activeFeature=import` renders the reviewed C23 import on its own with "Back to setup"; the wizard resumes afterwards. Test: wizard.test (import route) | `app.tsx`, `copy.ts`, P29 |
| R6 Academy step could not complete the device flow | The step embeds the reviewed `AcademyAccount` component (start, open the verification page, pending, completing, failure with retry, cancel, sign-out). Tests: boards R2On06, wizard flow | `wizard.tsx` |
| R7 transition outcomes ignored | Welcome advances only on an admitted `setOnboarding`; completion is one intent (`completeTenantSetup`) and closes only when the core confirms; refusals, failed and unknown deliveries stay visible with Retry. Tests: wizard.test (refusal on Welcome; refused/unknown completion with Retry) | `wizard.tsx` |
| R8 Back on the first step | Back is omitted on a mode's first step; `go` is bounded. Tests: boards (welcome, add) | `wizard.tsx` |
| R9 products could be emptied; summary omitted Runtime | Runtime Security is checked and disabled ("Always on"); the core keeps it first (`chooseSetupProducts`); the summary lists the core's products. Tests: core, boards R2On03/R2On07 | `wizard.tsx`, `setup_domain.rs` |
| R10 sheet exceeded the viewport | The modal is bounded (`max-height: 92vh`, scrolls inside); the sheet's height is `min(780px, 84vh)`; native N06 checks Cancel is inside the window at 900×600 once focused | `modal.tsx`, `wizard.tsx` |
| R11 missing screen content | Environment select (production/staging/other) on the profile and in the switcher/palette identity; optional Gateway workspace section (list → choose → endpoint + key); per-product starter packs with counts (`setup.packs`, imported by product at completion); licence state replaced by what each product reads with plus its verify result, with the note that licensing is not readable through the public APIs (P31); add mode makes the scan key optional (P17) | `features.rs`, `tenants.rs`, `wizard.tsx`, `copy.ts`, P28, P31 |
| R12 `recordedSecs` generated as bigint | `SetupWarning.recorded_secs` is `u32` (a JSON number); the validator requires a non-negative integer; core and host tests round-trip a populated warning | `features.rs`, `client.ts` |
| E1 T09 evidence | N06: every step and the sheet captured light/dark at 100%/200%, keyboard walks per step, the 900×600 sheet check | `acceptance_c29.py` |
| E2 tests validated the reduced implementation | Core, host, vitest and native checks rewritten for the draft/verify/complete contract (see each row) | tests |
| E3 contradictory secret contract | C29.md's acceptance row now states the P25 model and names the host test that proves confinement | `docs/planning/chunks/C29.md` |
| Optional: strings in copy.ts | Verify summaries, product cards, saved-state words and outcome texts moved to `copy.ts` | `copy.ts` |
| Optional: request.json references | The packet's limitations name only records that exist | `chain-c29.sh` |

B1 (live Vulture verify) stays blocked: the approved manifest designates Vulture for scans only; `evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md` names the family the owner must add. Nothing was run against Vulture.
